{"severity":"error","file":"errors/pure_violation_1.march","start_line":22,"start_col":2,"end_line":22,"end_col":20,"message":"`mod LeakyPure` (declared `cap pure`) declares `needs IO.FileWrite`, but a pure module cannot hold a capability: `needs` exists only to admit side effects, directly or through a stdlib wrapper such as `File.read` or `DateTime.now`.\n\nRemove the `needs` line, and move the code that needs it to a module without `cap pure`.","code":"pure_violation","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CONTRACT"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/pure_violation_1.march","start_line":26,"start_col":4,"end_line":26,"end_col":14,"message":"`write` in `mod LeakyPure` (declared `cap pure`) calls `file_write`, which has side effects.\n\nUse pure functions (no IO, spawn, vault, clock, or random ops) in a `cap pure` module.","code":"pure_violation","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CONTRACT"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/pure_violation_1.march","start_line":26,"start_col":4,"end_line":26,"end_col":30,"message":"expected `Result((), String)` but got `Result((), FileError)`.","code":"type_mismatch","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/pure_violation_1.march","start_line":25,"start_col":2,"end_line":27,"end_col":5,"message":"the expected type comes from here"}],"notes":["This is the declared return type of `write`.","The types differ here:\n    Result((), FileError)\n               ^^^^^^^^^ expected `String`"],"category":"TYPE MISMATCH"}
